# modules/iac/terraform.rules - docs/DESIGN.md §8.2 IaC seed catalog, scoped to
# Terraform HCL only (docs/DESIGN.md §13 step 4, this ticket).
#
# Path note: rules/RULE-FORMAT.md §9's frozen path table grants the
# pattern-rule schema to `modules/iac/*.rules` FLAT - unlike
# `modules/sast/rules/*.rules`, there is no `rules/` subdirectory under
# modules/iac/.  A file at modules/iac/rules/terraform.rules would match no
# row of that table and fail E070.  The basename `checks.rules` is reserved
# repository-wide for the §9.5 script-check schema (it is matched first in
# records_schema_for_path, ahead of the `modules/iac/*.rules` row), so this
# pack is deliberately named `terraform.rules`, never `checks.rules`.
#
# Scope discipline: Terraform (*.tf) only, per this ticket.  CloudFormation,
# Docker, Kubernetes, and Helm checks - though §8.2 and this same `.rules`
# engine could carry them - are explicitly out of scope here; see
# docs/DESIGN.md §8.2's own "Optional adapter" note and §7 (containers) for
# where those belong instead.
#
# Seed rules, each straight out of §8.2's list:
#   cidr_blocks = ["0.0.0.0/0"], acl = "public-read", encrypted = false,
#   missing enable_key_rotation, associate_public_ip_address = true,
#   hardcoded secrets in .tf, publicly_accessible = true (RDS).
#
# IAC-TF-OPEN_CIDR-01 is rules/RULE-FORMAT.md §9.1.1's own worked example and
# §12.5's own worked pattern-rule example; both are reproduced here verbatim
# rather than paraphrased, so this pack matches the spec's own reference
# byte-for-byte.
#
# IAC-TF-KEY_ROTATION_DISABLED-01 is the one ABSENCE check in this pack, the
# same shape java.rules' SAST-JAVA-XXE_DISALLOW_DOCTYPE-01 already
# establishes: the finding fires on `resource "aws_kms_key" ...  {` unless a
# `enable_key_rotation = true` line appears within the context-window.  Like
# that precedent, an absence check can only be a `context-deny` with a
# non-zero window (rules/RULE-FORMAT.md §10.2 - context-window:0 binds
# same-line-intent guards only), so it carries the same reviewed W033
# trade-off; the window (12 lines) is sized to the typical short
# `aws_kms_key` resource block.

id: IAC-TF-OPEN_CIDR-01
title: Security group rule open to 0.0.0.0/0
severity: high
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-284
owasp: A02:2025
pattern: cidr_blocks\s*=\s*\[[^]]*"0\.0\.0\.0/0"
dialect: ere
files: *.tf
context-deny: ^\s*#\s*scoursh-allow: open-cidr
context-window: 1
tags: static
tags: compliance
cis: 5.2
cis: 5.3
remediation: Restrict the CIDR to the smallest network that needs access.
  Where public reachability is genuinely required (a public load balancer listener),
  terminate it at an edge that applies WAF and rate limiting rather than at the
  instance security group, and record the exception with an inline
  "# scoursh-allow: open-cidr" comment on the preceding line.
references: CIS-AWS-5.2

id: IAC-TF-PUBLIC_ACL-01
title: S3 bucket ACL set to a public value
severity: critical
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-284
owasp: A02:2025
pattern: acl\s*=\s*"public-read(-write)?"
dialect: ere
files: *.tf
tags: static
tags: compliance
cis: 2.1.1
remediation: Remove the public ACL and rely on the bucket's default private ACL with
  Block Public Access enabled. If the object truly must be public, front it with
  CloudFront and an Origin Access Control instead of a public bucket ACL.
references: CWE-284
references: CIS-AWS-2.1.1

id: IAC-TF-UNENCRYPTED-01
title: Resource explicitly configured without encryption at rest
severity: high
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-311
owasp: A04:2025
pattern: \bencrypted\s*=\s*false\b
dialect: ere
files: *.tf
tags: static
tags: compliance
cis: 2.1.1
remediation: Set encrypted = true (or omit the attribute where the provider default is
  encryption-on) and, where the resource supports it, pin a customer-managed KMS key
  rather than relying on the provider default key.
references: CWE-311

id: IAC-TF-KEY_ROTATION_DISABLED-01
title: KMS key created without automatic key rotation enabled
severity: medium
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-320
owasp: A04:2025
pattern: resource\s+"aws_kms_key"\s+"[A-Za-z0-9_-]+"\s*\{
dialect: ere
files: *.tf
context-deny: enable_key_rotation\s*=\s*true
context-window: 12
tags: static
remediation: Add enable_key_rotation = true to the aws_kms_key resource so AWS rotates
  the backing key material annually without any application-visible change (KMS
  transparently keeps prior key material available for decrypting old ciphertext).
references: CWE-320
references: CIS-AWS-3.8
cis: 3.8

id: IAC-TF-PUBLIC_IP-01
title: Instance or launch resource auto-assigns a public IP address
severity: high
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-284
owasp: A02:2025
pattern: associate_public_ip_address\s*=\s*true
dialect: ere
files: *.tf
tags: static
tags: compliance
remediation: Set associate_public_ip_address = false and reach the instance through a
  bastion, a VPN, or a load balancer in a public subnet instead of giving the
  instance itself a public address. If a public address is genuinely required,
  pair it with a security group scoped to specific source ranges, not 0.0.0.0/0.
references: CWE-284

id: IAC-TF-HARDCODED_SECRET-01
title: Hardcoded credential literal in Terraform configuration
severity: critical
confidence: medium
cwe: CWE-798
owasp: A07:2025
pattern: \b(password|secret|secret_key|access_key|api_key|token)\s*=\s*"[^"$]{8,}"
dialect: ere
files: *.tf
context-deny: (CHANGEME|changeme|EXAMPLE|example|XXXXXXXX|xxxxxxxx|placeholder|dummy|TODO)
context-window: 0
tags: static
remediation: Remove the literal credential from the .tf file and rotate it immediately;
  a committed secret must be treated as compromised even if the commit is later
  reverted, because it remains in git history. Source the value from a variable backed
  by a secret store (Vault, AWS Secrets Manager, SSM SecureString) instead of a literal.
references: CWE-798

id: IAC-TF-RDS_PUBLIC-01
title: RDS instance configured as publicly accessible
severity: critical
confidence: high
cwe: CWE-284
owasp: A02:2025
pattern: publicly_accessible\s*=\s*true
dialect: ere
files: *.tf
tags: static
tags: compliance
cis: 2.3.2
remediation: Set publicly_accessible = false and reach the database through an
  application tier inside the same VPC, a bastion, or a VPN, never a public endpoint.
references: CWE-284
references: CIS-AWS-2.3.2
